        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          {% image "/assets/images/antonello-comandante.jpg", "Antonello Budini Gattai at the controls of an Airbus A321", "(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw", "rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover" %}
        </div>

        <div class="md:col-span-2 flex flex-col justify-center">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
            Antonello Budini Gattai
          </h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
            <p class="mb-4">
              The airfield was born from the passion of <strong>Antonello Budini Gattai</strong>, a former Alitalia Comandante,
              who after retirement chose to return to his family's countryside where, as a fifteen-year-old,
              he used to fly his model aircraft.
            </p>
            <p>
              Today this vision lives on in <strong>Gliding in Tuscany</strong>, the aerial farm stay at Podere Sant'Apollonia,
              nestled in the Val di Chiana, just minutes from Castiglion Fiorentino and Cortona. Here nature,
              rural hospitality and aviation come together in a unique place, where a grass airstrip among
              sunflowers welcomes pilots and enthusiasts from around the world.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center mb-12">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">A career among the clouds</h3>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Trained at the Aero Club of Florence, Antonello began his professional career in 1968
            with Società Aerea Mediterranea, flying for over thirty years until becoming an Alitalia Comandante.
          </p>
          <p>
            Alongside his airline career, he pursued sport and glider flying, participating in international
            competitions and rallies, and earning the highest honours from the International Aeronautical Federation.
          </p>
        </div>

        {% image "/assets/images/antonello-storia.jpg", "Antonello Budini Gattai - his 1963 flight logbook and with a glider model", "(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw", "rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full object-cover" %}
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center mb-12">
        {% image "/assets/images/antonello-aereo.jpg", "Antonello Budini Gattai next to the tow plane", "(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw", "rounded-lg shadow-lg w-full aspect-[4/3] object-cover" %}
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">The return to Tuscany</h3>
          <p>
            Having returned to Tuscany for good, he brought his family's estate back to life, transforming it
            into a place where you can experience the landscape from above and from the ground: apartments
            set within the historic Leopoldina farmhouse, flying activities, aeronautical events and authentic
            hospitality, guided by experience, discretion and a deep love for the land. Here every guest is
            invited to discover Tuscany with the same spirit with which Antonello continues, to this day, to fly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
